{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0018_diacritic_write_commands_warn_on_non_normalizing_forms", "label": "ADR 0018: diacritic write commands warn on forms that do not match their key", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0018-diacritic-write-commands-warn-on-non-normalizing-forms.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "status": "proposed", "rationale": "diacritic add, delete, and diacritic-disambiguate can store entries whose display form does not normalize to the key, the same inconsistency the old variant-to-headword builder wrote (acmuman to \u0101-cuman). A hard reject would block legitimate curated variants such as blac stored as bl\u00e6c/bl\u01e3c. The commands warn and confirm, and --yes skips the prompt on add. Frontmatter remains proposed; the body says this is implemented."}, {"id": "non_normalizing_form_warning", "label": "Non-normalizing macron-index form warning", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0018-diacritic-write-commands-warn-on-non-normalizing-forms.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "add and the disambiguate actions replace unique, add attested form, and choose a candidate warn when normalize_old_english of the stored form is not the key. Hyphens, eth/thorn, case, and marks alone do not warn. The entry cannot be applied to text and will only show up in .unaligned. Confirmation is required because curated variants whose letters differ from the headword are legitimate. An audit of existing mismatches is deferred, not rejected."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0018_diacritic_write_commands_warn_on_non_normalizing_forms", "target": "docs_adr_0016_macron_index_variants_are_own_entries_and_index_is_repaired_not_regenerated", "relation": "follows", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0018-diacritic-write-commands-warn-on-non-normalizi